---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" updated="September 2026">
  <p><em>This notice explains what we collect and why. It is written to align with India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023. It is general information, not legal advice — please have it reviewed for your specific situation.</em></p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} is the data fiduciary responsible for the personal data described here. For any privacy request or question, contact us at {SITE.email}.</p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Purchase email:</strong> the email you provide at checkout, used to deliver your download link and receipt.</li>
    <li><strong>Order details:</strong> the project purchased, amount, and payment reference from Razorpay.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact messages:</strong> the name, email and message you submit via the contact form.</li>
    <li><strong>Basic technical data:</strong> standard server logs and, where enabled, privacy-friendly bot protection (Cloudflare Turnstile).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What we do not collect</h2>
  <p>We never see or store your card numbers, UPI IDs, or banking credentials — these are handled entirely by Razorpay. We do not sell your data or share it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>4. Why we use it (purpose &amp; consent)</h2>
  <p>We use your data only for the specific purpose you gave it for: processing an order and delivering your files (to fulfil your purchase), replying to a contact message (to answer you), and — only if you separately opt in — sending occasional project updates. We ask for your consent at the point of collection and do not bundle unrelated purposes.</p>

  <h2>5. Withdrawing consent</h2>
  <p>You can withdraw consent or unsubscribe at any time by contacting us at {SITE.email}. Withdrawing consent does not affect processing already carried out, and we may still keep the minimum records the law requires (for example, tax and accounting records for completed orders).</p>

  <h2>6. Third parties</h2>
  <p>We rely on <strong>Razorpay</strong> (payments), <strong>Brevo</strong> (transactional email), <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (hosting, storage and security), and affiliate stores you choose to visit. Each has its own privacy policy governing data they process.</p>

  <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
  <p>Order records are retained as required for accounting and support. Contact messages and other personal data are deleted on request where we are not legally required to keep them.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data, and you may nominate someone to exercise your rights. To make a request, contact us and we will respond within a reasonable time.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>This service is directed at a general audience and is not intended for children under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal data from minors. If you believe a minor has provided personal data, contact us and we will delete it. Where children's data is involved, applicable law requires verifiable parental consent.</p>

  <h2>10. Grievances</h2>
  <p>If you have a concern about how your data is handled, contact our grievance point at {SITE.email}. We take privacy complaints seriously and will work to resolve them promptly.</p>

  <h2>11. Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use only essential cookies and local storage (security, session integrity such as CSRF protection, and remembering that you've dismissed the cookie notice). See our <a href="/legal/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>. We do not use third-party advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>For privacy requests, reach us via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or at {SITE.email}.</p>
</Legal>
